  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Polka style of the Slovenian-American neighbourhoods of Cleveland, Ohio, which reworked Slovenian folk tunes and dance songs into a smooth, swinging American dance-band sound; Frankie Yankovic's 1948 Columbia hit 'Just Because' made it nationally popular, alongside the accordionists Johnny Pecon and Lou Trebar. The lead is a piano or button accordion, often doubled by a saxophone in close harmony, over a banjo chording on the offbeats, bass and drums, with vocals in English or Slovenian.",
